cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this lab or its data in your work, please cite both the manuscript and this software release."
type: software
title: "bft-uav-validation-lab"
abstract: >-
  Empirical validation testbed for the IEEE Access manuscript
  "Byzantine-Fault-Tolerant Hierarchical Navigation for GNSS-Denied UAV
  Swarms: Architecture, Theoretical Analysis, and Empirical Validation"
  (Kalynovskyi, 2026). The lab provides a ROS 2 + Gazebo + Python harness,
  18 ROS 2 nodes, 18 message types, sweep scripts, Docker recipes, and the
  production-sweep raw data for every numerical claim in Sections VI and
  VII of the manuscript. Every paper number is traceable to a workspace
  file via CODE_TO_CLAIM_MAPPING.md.
